              "id": "04493dd9-bcf9-3937-87fa-0d77019df894",
              "name": "Prototype Pollution Vulnerability Detected",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "## Description\n\nPrototype Pollution is a vulnerability that occurs when the properties of JavaScript's object prototype are manipulated. The prototype is an object that is associated with every function and object by default in JavaScript, which can be modified to add properties and methods that can be used by all instances of that object. The Prototype Pollution vulnerability can lead to several issues such as Denial of Service (DoS), Remote Code Execution, and even property injection.\n\nThe provided JavaScript code snippet is vulnerable to Prototype Pollution as it allows the modification of a prototype object. If an attacker can control part of the structure passed to this function, they can add or modify a property that will then exist on all objects parsed by your code.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\nTo mitigate Prototype Pollution vulnerabilities, follow these general guidelines:\n\n- Avoid using user input to directly modify object properties.\n- Use input validation to ensure that user input is as expected.\n- Use Object.freeze() to prevent new properties from being added to objects.\n- Use Object.seal() to prevent new properties from being added or existing properties from being removed.\n- Use Object.preventExtensions() to prevent new properties from being added to an object.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nThe specific fix for the provided code snippet would depend on the exact requirements of your application. However, a general fix would be to validate the input to ensure it does not contain any properties that should not be modified. For example:\n\n```javascript\nif (typeof i !== \"string\" || !i.includes('__proto__') || !i.includes('prototype') || !i.includes('constructor')) {\n    if (y === i) {\n        F = true;\n        break;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## Library Dependencies\n\nThe provided code snippet does not appear to have any specific library dependencies.\n\n## References\n\n- [CWE-250: Execution with Unnecessary Privileges](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/250.html)\n\nPlease note that the links provided are active and accessible to anonymous users at the time of writing."
              },
