            {
              "id": "3e0f8006-44d4-3f2d-bda8-c05fcd130a93",
              "name": "\"Potential XSS Vulnerability from User-Controlled Data in HTML String\"",
              "helpUri": "https://www.glog.ai/",
              "help": {
                "text": "",
                "markdown": "The provided code snippet appears to be vulnerable to a Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) attack. This type of vulnerability occurs when an application includes untrusted data in a new web page without proper validation or escaping, or updates an existing web page with user-supplied data using a browser API that can create HTML or JavaScript. XSS allows attackers to execute scripts in the victim's browser which can hijack user sessions, deface web sites, or redirect the user to malicious sites.\n\nIn this specific case, the vulnerability arises from user-controlled data in an HTML string. If an attacker can control a value that is written directly to HTML, they can include arbitrary HTML content (e.g., script elements), leading to an XSS vulnerability.\n\n## Mitigation Advice\n\n1. **Escape User Input**: Always escape user-controlled data before displaying it on your pages. This ensures that any HTML special characters (like `<`, `>`, `&`, etc.) are displayed as they are, and not interpreted as HTML tags or entities.\n\n2. **Use Safe APIs**: Use functions that explicitly make the data safe for a given context. For example, use `element.textContent` (not `element.innerHTML`), or use parameterized SQL and prepared statements.\n\n3. **Content Security Policy (CSP)**: Implementing CSP helps in reducing the risk of XSS attacks as it allows web developers to control the resources which a user agent is allowed to load on a page.\n\n## Source Code Fix Recommendation\n\nWithout the full context of the code, it's hard to provide a specific fix. However, a general recommendation would be to escape any user-controlled data that is being written to the page. For example, if you're using jQuery, you could replace:\n\n```javascript\nelement.html(userControlledData);\n```\n\nwith:\n\n```javascript\nelement.text(userControlledData);\n```\n\n## Dependencies\n\nThe code appears to be using the jQuery library.\n\n## References\n\n- [OWASP XSS Prevention Cheat Sheet](https://cheatsheetseries.owasp.org/cheatsheets/Cross_Site_Scripting_Prevention_Cheat_Sheet.html)\n- [CWE-79: Improper Neutralization of Input During Web Page Generation ('Cross-site Scripting')](https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html)"
              },
              "properties": {
                "cwe": [
                  {
                    "id": "CWE-79",
                    "url": "https://cwe.mitre.org/data/definitions/79.html"
                  }
                ],
                "severity": "MEDIUM",
                "kind": "FAIL",
                "tags": [
                  "CWE-79"
                ]
              }
